// Title: Wdigest Enable UseLogonCredential
// Sigma ID: d6a9b252-c666-4de6-8806-5561bbbd3bdc
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Roberto Rodriguez (Cyb3rWard0g), OTR (Open Threat Research)
// Date: 2019-09-12 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: persistence, defense-impairment, T1112
// Description: Detects potential malicious modification of the property value of UseLogonCredential from
//   HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\SecurityProviders\WDigest to enable clear-text
//   credentials
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://threathunterplaybook.com/hunts/windows/190510-RegModWDigestDowngrade/notebook.html
//   - https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/topic/microsoft-security-advisory-update-to-improve-credentials-protection-and-management-may-13-2014-93434251-04ac-b7f3-52aa-9f951c14b649
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/73fcfa1d4863f6a4e17f90e54401de6e30a312bb/atomics/T1112/T1112.md#atomic-test-3---modify-registry-to-store-logon-credentials
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_wdigest_enable_uselogoncredential.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "WDigest\\UseLogonCredential" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000001)"
